			<div class="content" id="post-content-4474638">
									

<p>Hi everyone.</p>
<p>A little hi from the french branch !</p>
<p>This is my entry for the SCP-5000 contest and also first contribution to the english wiki. It might be a little different from what you are used to here. But it sums up what I love in the Foundation. An organic universe, endlessly growing, bringing always more questions with each answer delivered. I hope some of you will enjoy it and follow the tips of good ol' Dr. Mústês to solve the riddles surrounding this bloody tower ! For the most determined among you, all the answers will be delivered. Actually, most of them already are. Good hunt !</p>
<p>I'd like to thank <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drmacro" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3296783); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3296783&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1579563937" alt="DrMacro" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3296783)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drmacro" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3296783); return false;">DrMacro</a></span> for his help on translating SCP-038-FR, since it was in this article but not available in english yet.</p>
<p>I'd like to thank <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/archiviste-judas" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2997441); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2997441&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1579563937" alt="Archiviste Judas" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2997441)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/archiviste-judas" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2997441); return false;">Archiviste Judas</a></span> for his help with the formating review.</p>
<p>I'd also like to thank <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/seyph" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4742038); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4742038&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1579563937" alt="Seyph" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4742038)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/seyph" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4742038); return false;">Seyph</a></span> for her incredible fanart of the events described in this entry. Here is the <a href="https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/344973115303919619/668557894257737728/boucle.png?width=380&amp;height=676">fanart</a>.</p>
<p>I thought I will never be on time to post this entry, since I kinda only had some free time last week to write it and translate it. If you spot some errors, feel free to correct them (if you're willing to of course !).</p>
<p>As needed, here are my top 5 slots :</p>
<p>SCP-5999<br />
SCP-5555<br />
SCP-5001<br />
SCP-5790</p>
<p>Enjoy the reading <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">I hope</span> !</p>
<p>PS : I'm currently trying hard to translate 312-FR, it should be available in a correct version tomorrow night. But the article isn't essential to the comprehension of the SCP, it's more an easter egg. It also explains deeper what a Tennenti Hole is. You'll have it tomorrow, sorry for the inconvenience.</p>

